cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ChromaPilot, please cite both the software and the paper below."
title: "ChromaPilot: an LLM agent for multiplexed epigenomics analysis"
abstract: >-
  ChromaPilot turns a plain-language request into a reviewed, executed and
  documented epigenomics analysis. It plans the pipeline, shows the plan for
  human review before anything runs, executes it with a validated tool library,
  generates and self-corrects code when no tool fits, and produces a
  reproducible script and a PDF report. Hiplex CUT&Tag and ChIP-DIP are
  supported end to end.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/J041120h/chromaPilot"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.22549678"
    description: "Demo Data for ChromaPilot (concept DOI — always resolves to the latest version)"
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.22753661"
    description: "Demo Data for ChromaPilot (version 2)"
keywords:
  - epigenomics
  - CUT&Tag
  - ChIP-DIP
  - LLM agent
  - bioinformatics workflow
  - reproducible research

